---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Documentation & Architecture | NNUI-KIT" activePath="/docs">
  <div class="docs-layout-container">
    <!-- Left Navigation Sidebar -->
    <aside class="docs-aside">
      <div class="docs-aside-group">
        <div class="docs-aside-title">Getting Started</div>
        <a href="#introduction" class="docs-aside-link active">Introduction</a>
        <a href="#mental-model" class="docs-aside-link">Three-Tier Architecture</a>
        <a href="/shadow-vs-light" class="docs-aside-link" style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; color: #10b981; font-weight: 600;">
          <span>Light vs Shadow DOM</span>
          <span style="font-size: 0.65rem; background: rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.15); color: #10b981; padding: 1px 5px; border-radius: 9999px;">WHY</span>
        </a>
        <a href="#why-light-dom" class="docs-aside-link">Why Light-DOM?</a>
        <a href="#installation" class="docs-aside-link">Installation & Setup</a>
      </div>


      <div class="docs-aside-group">
        <div class="docs-aside-title">Crown Innovations</div>
        <a href="#persistence" class="docs-aside-link">Declarative Persistence</a>
        <a href="#cross-tab" class="docs-aside-link">Cross-Tab Broadcast Sync</a>
        <a href="#ai-introspection" class="docs-aside-link">AI Introspection Protocol</a>
        <a href="/llms" class="docs-aside-link" style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; color: var(--brand-400, #818cf8);">
          <span>llms.txt (AI Spec)</span>
          <span style="font-size: 0.65rem; background: rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.2); color: var(--brand-400, #818cf8); padding: 1px 5px; border-radius: 9999px; font-weight: 700;">NEW</span>
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="docs-aside-group">
        <div class="docs-aside-title">Design System & Tokens</div>
        <a href="#typography-system" class="docs-aside-link">Typography System</a>
        <a href="#layout-primitives" class="docs-aside-link">Layout & Status Primitives</a>
        <a href="/tokens" class="docs-aside-link">Theme Studio (Live)</a>
        <a href="/typography" class="docs-aside-link">Typography Studio ↗</a>
      </div>

      <div class="docs-aside-group">
        <div class="docs-aside-title">Framework Adapters</div>
        <a href="#react" class="docs-aside-link">React 18 & 19</a>
        <a href="#svelte" class="docs-aside-link">Svelte 5 (Runes)</a>
        <a href="#vue" class="docs-aside-link">Vue 3</a>
        <a href="#htmx" class="docs-aside-link">HTMX 2 & Backend SSR</a>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <!-- Main Docs Content -->
    <main class="docs-body">
      <!-- Introduction -->
      <section id="introduction" style="margin-bottom: 4rem;">
        <h1 style="font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.03em; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--text-main);">
          Introduction & Architecture
        </h1>
        <p style="font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
          NNUI-KIT is a platform-native, three-tier Light-DOM universal UI system. It delivers accessible, composable interface components that execute identically across every modern web framework with zero Shadow DOM barriers and sub-40 KB runtime footprint.
        </p>

        <!-- 3-Tier Architecture Flow -->
        <div id="mental-model" data-ui="card" style="border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 12px; padding: 2rem; background: var(--bg-card); margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
          <h2 style="font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 700; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; color: var(--text-main);">Three-Tier Architecture</h2>
          
          <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem;">
            <div data-ui="card" style="padding: 1.25rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 8px; background: var(--bg-secondary);">
              <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">
                <strong style="color: var(--text-main); font-size: 0.95rem;">Tier 0: Pure Semantic Primitives (17 Zero-JS Controls)</strong>
                <span class="docs-version-pill" data-ui="badge">Zero JS</span>
              </div>
              <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-muted);">
                Buttons, Badges, Inputs, Checkboxes, Switches, Cards, Skeletons, Dividers, Grid & Stack layouts. Render instantly via CSS Cascade Layers (<code>@layer ui.base</code>).
              </p>
            </div>

            <div data-ui="card" style="padding: 1.25rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 8px; background: var(--bg-secondary);">
              <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">
                <strong style="color: var(--text-main); font-size: 0.95rem;">Tier 1: Design Tokens & CSS Cascade Layers</strong>
                <span class="docs-version-pill" data-ui="badge">W3C DTCG</span>
              </div>
              <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-muted);">
                W3C DTCG tokens specification with 6 color palettes (Zinc, Slate, Neutral, Violet, Rose, Emerald). Layered defensively across <code>@layer ui.tokens, ui.base, ui.components, ui.overrides</code>.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div data-ui="card" style="padding: 1.25rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 8px; background: var(--bg-secondary);">
              <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">
                <strong style="color: var(--text-main); font-size: 0.95rem;">Tier 2: Micro-Enhancers (28 Light-DOM Custom Elements)</strong>
                <span class="docs-version-pill" data-ui="badge" style="border-color: #10b981; color: #10b981;">Sub-40 KB</span>
              </div>
              <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-muted);">
                Virtualized Data Grid (>15k rows), Date Range Picker, Combobox, Dialog, Stepper, AI Prompt Box, Tabs. 100% Light-DOM custom elements with <code>ElementInternals</code> form association.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Why Light-DOM? Table -->
      <section id="why-light-dom" style="margin-bottom: 4rem;">
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.75rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--text-main);">
          Why Light-DOM? (Solving Shadow DOM Traps)
        </h2>
        <p style="font-size: 1rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
          Traditional Web Component libraries seal templates inside closed Shadow DOM roots. While isolation sounds good initially, it creates severe accessibility, styling, and form participation bottlenecks in production applications:
        </p>

        <div style="overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 10px; background: var(--bg-card);">
          <table data-ui="table" class="ui-table" style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.9rem; text-align: left;">
            <thead>
              <tr style="background: var(--bg-secondary); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);">
                <th style="padding: 0.85rem 1.25rem;">Dimension</th>
                <th style="padding: 0.85rem 1.25rem; color: #ef4444;">Shadow DOM Libraries</th>
                <th style="padding: 0.85rem 1.25rem; color: #10b981;">NNUI-KIT (Light-DOM)</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);">
                <td style="padding: 0.85rem 1.25rem; font-weight: 600;">Global CSS & Tailwind</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.85rem 1.25rem; color: var(--text-muted);">Blocked by boundary (requires ::part())</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.85rem 1.25rem; color: var(--text-main);">Directly styled by standard classes & @layer cascade</td>
              </tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);">
                <td style="padding: 0.85rem 1.25rem; font-weight: 600;">Form Participation</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.85rem 1.25rem; color: var(--text-muted);">Requires synthetic hidden input injection hacks</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.85rem 1.25rem; color: var(--text-main);">Native ElementInternals & FormData auto-serialization</td>
              </tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);">
                <td style="padding: 0.85rem 1.25rem; font-weight: 600;">Screen Readers (A11y)</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.85rem 1.25rem; color: var(--text-muted);">Fragmented accessibility tree; broken aria-labelledby IDs</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.85rem 1.25rem; color: var(--text-main);">Unbroken DOM tree; standard document ID references</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td style="padding: 0.85rem 1.25rem; font-weight: 600;">Framework V-DOM</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.85rem 1.25rem; color: var(--text-muted);">Hydration mismatch and node duplication conflicts</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.85rem 1.25rem; color: var(--text-main);">"Mutate Attributes, Never Nodes" — 100% V-DOM safe</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Installation & Quickstart -->
      <section id="installation" style="margin-bottom: 4rem;">
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.75rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--text-main);">
          Installation & Setup
        </h2>
        <p style="font-size: 1rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
          Install via npm or use the registry CLI to drop zero-dependency custom elements and copy-pasteable CSS theme tokens directly into your project:
        </p>
        <pre class="code-viewer-pre" style="border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); margin-bottom: 1.5rem;"><code># 1. Install universal package
npm install nnuikit

# 2. Or initialize the CLI (automatically generates theme.css and tokens in your app)
npx nnui init

# 3. Add components with your specific framework target:
npx nnui add dialog --react   # Drops React compound component into src/components/ui/
npx nnui add dialog --html    # Drops vanilla HTML snippet & JS micro-enhancer
npx nnui add dialog --rails   # Drops Rails ERB partial & configures importmap.rb</code></pre>

        <!-- Framework Targets Card -->
        <div data-ui="card" style="border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--bg-card); margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
            <div style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-main); font-size: 1rem; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem;">
              <span>🚀</span>
              <span>Framework Targets: True Code Ownership Across Stacks</span>
            </div>
            <span class="docs-version-pill" style="border-color: #6366f1; color: #6366f1;">CLI v1.0.5</span>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0 1rem;">
            Unlike shadcn/ui (locked to React) or traditional web components (locked in Shadow DOM), NNUI-KIT provides <strong>100% Light-DOM code ownership</strong> across modern frontend and server-rendered stacks. Run the CLI with your framework target:
          </p>

          <ui-tabs value="react" style="width: 100%; display: block;">
            <div data-part="tablist" style="display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding-bottom: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; overflow-x: auto;">
              <button data-part="tab" data-value="react" style="padding: 0.4rem 0.85rem; border-radius: 6px; border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); background: var(--bg-canvas); color: var(--text-main); font-size: 0.82rem; font-weight: 600; cursor: pointer;">
                ⚛️ React / Next.js (--react)
              </button>
              <button data-part="tab" data-value="html" style="padding: 0.4rem 0.85rem; border-radius: 6px; border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); background: var(--bg-canvas); color: var(--text-main); font-size: 0.82rem; font-weight: 600; cursor: pointer;">
                🌐 Vanilla HTML (--html)
              </button>
              <button data-part="tab" data-value="rails" style="padding: 0.4rem 0.85rem; border-radius: 6px; border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); background: var(--bg-canvas); color: var(--text-main); font-size: 0.82rem; font-weight: 600; cursor: pointer;">
                💎 Ruby on Rails (--rails)
              </button>
            </div>

            <!-- React Tab -->
            <div data-part="tabpanel" data-value="react">
              <pre class="code-viewer-pre" style="border-radius: 6px; font-size: 0.8rem; padding: 1rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><code>{`# Drops React 18/19 compound component into src/components/ui/dialog.jsx
npx nnui add dialog --react

// In your application:
import { Dialog, DialogModal } from './components/ui/dialog.jsx';

export function Example() {
  return (
    <DialogModal open={isOpen} onClose={() => setIsOpen(false)} title="Confirm Release">
      <p>You own the markup and internals!</p>
    </DialogModal>
  );
}`}</code></pre>
              <p style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 0;">
                Exports raw primitives, typed compound subcomponents (<code style="color: var(--ui-color-brand-500);">Dialog.Trigger</code>, <code style="color: var(--ui-color-brand-500);">Dialog.Content</code>, <code style="color: var(--ui-color-brand-500);">Dialog.Close</code>), and an editable composite modal.
              </p>
            </div>

            <!-- HTML Tab -->
            <div data-part="tabpanel" data-value="html">
              <pre class="code-viewer-pre" style="border-radius: 6px; font-size: 0.8rem; padding: 1rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><code>{`# Drops runnable HTML snippet & JS micro-enhancer into components/ui/dialog/
npx nnui add dialog --html

<!-- components/ui/dialog/dialog.html -->
<ui-dialog id="my-modal">
  <button data-part="trigger" type="button">Open Modal</button>
  <dialog data-part="dialog">
    <div data-part="panel">
      <h3>Platform Top-Layer Modal</h3>
      <p>Zero build step, 100% accessible.</p>
      <button data-part="close" type="button">Close</button>
    </div>
  </dialog>
</ui-dialog>

<script type="module" src="./ui-dialog.js"></script>`}</code></pre>
              <p style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 0;">
                Includes standalone micro-enhancer and semantic Light-DOM HTML snippet. Open directly in any browser.
              </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Rails Tab -->
            <div data-part="tabpanel" data-value="rails">
              <pre class="code-viewer-pre" style="border-radius: 6px; font-size: 0.8rem; padding: 1rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><code>{`# Generates ERB partial, asset pipeline JS, and pins nnuikit in importmap.rb
npx nnui add dialog --rails

<%# app/views/pages/home.html.erb %>
<%= render "components/dialog", id: "confirm-modal", title: "Canary Rollout" do %>
  <p>Rendered with native Rails ERB and Light-DOM web components.</p>
<% end %>`}</code></pre>
              <p style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 0;">
                Creates <code style="color: var(--ui-color-brand-500);">app/views/components/_dialog.html.erb</code> with <code style="color: var(--ui-color-brand-500);">local_assigns</code> and block yields, and configures Rails Importmaps automatically.
              </p>
            </div>
          </ui-tabs>
        </div>

        <!-- Global CSS Theme Callout Box -->
        <div data-ui="card" style="border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--bg-card); margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
            <div style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-main); font-size: 1rem; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem;">
              <span>🎨</span>
              <span>Theme & Global CSS Tokens (Turnkey Copy-Paste)</span>
            </div>
            <a href="/tokens" data-ui="button" data-variant="secondary" data-size="xs" style="text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.78rem; padding: 0.35rem 0.85rem;">
              Theme Studio & Exporter →
            </a>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0 1rem;">
            NNUI-KIT provides standalone, W3C DTCG-compliant global CSS theme files. You can import them directly from the package, or copy-paste them straight into your product's <code style="color: var(--ui-color-brand-500);">globals.css</code> or <code style="color: var(--ui-color-brand-500);">theme.css</code>:
          </p>

          <pre class="code-viewer-pre" style="border-radius: 6px; font-size: 0.8rem; padding: 1rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;"><code>// Option 1: Full Universal Stylesheet (Cascade layers, tokens, reset & base primitives)
import 'nnuikit/globals.css';

// Option 2: Pure Theme Custom Properties (Zero-dependency CSS variables only)
import 'nnuikit/theme.css';</code></pre>

          <p style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 0;">
            Want to customize brand color harmonies, light/dark modes, and border radii? Visit our <a href="/tokens" style="color: var(--ui-color-brand-500); font-weight: 600; text-decoration: underline;">Design Tokens & Theme Studio</a> to test components in real time and copy or download your tailored CSS theme file with 1 click.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Crown Innovations -->
      <section id="persistence" style="margin-bottom: 4rem;">
        <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
          <h2 style="font-size: 1.75rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 0; color: var(--text-main);">
            Crown Innovation: Declarative State Persistence
          </h2>
          <span class="docs-version-pill" style="border-color: #10b981; color: #10b981;">Zero Router Boilerplate</span>
        </div>
        <p style="font-size: 1rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
          Eliminate hundreds of lines of router boilerplate by adding declarative persistence attributes directly to your markup. State automatically hydrates on page load and reflects live changes:
        </p>
        <pre class="code-viewer-pre" style="border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); margin-bottom: 1rem;"><code>&lt;!-- Automatically binds search, column sort, and pagination to URL query params --&gt;
&lt;ui-data-grid persist="url"&gt;&lt;/ui-data-grid&gt;

&lt;!-- Autosaves multi-step wizard step and form values to localStorage --&gt;
&lt;ui-stepper persist="local"&gt;&lt;/ui-stepper&gt;

&lt;!-- Saves unfinished user drafts in AI prompt box --&gt;
&lt;ui-ai-prompt-box persist="local"&gt;&lt;/ui-ai-prompt-box&gt;</code></pre>
      </section>

      <!-- Cross-Tab Broadcast Sync -->
      <section id="cross-tab" style="margin-bottom: 4rem;">
        <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
          <h2 style="font-size: 1.75rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 0; color: var(--text-main);">
            Cross-Tab Broadcast Synchronization
          </h2>
          <span class="docs-version-pill" style="border-color: #10b981; color: #10b981;">Zero Server / Zero WebSockets</span>
        </div>
        <p style="font-size: 1rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
          Every NNUI-KIT micro-enhancer supports zero-config multi-tab synchronization powered by the native browser <code>BroadcastChannel</code> API. State updates in one tab instantly propagate to other open tabs:
        </p>
        <pre class="code-viewer-pre" style="border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); margin-bottom: 1rem;"><code>&lt;!-- Stepper synchronizes current active step across all open browser windows --&gt;
&lt;ui-stepper sync="cross-tab"&gt;
  &lt;div data-part="step" data-title="Account"&gt;...&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div data-part="step" data-title="Profile"&gt;...&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div data-part="step" data-title="Review"&gt;...&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/ui-stepper&gt;

&lt;!-- Combine URL persistence and Cross-Tab sync simultaneously --&gt;
&lt;ui-data-grid persist="url" sync="cross-tab"&gt;&lt;/ui-data-grid&gt;</code></pre>
      </section>

      <!-- AI Introspection Protocol -->
      <section id="ai-introspection" style="margin-bottom: 4rem;">
        <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
          <h2 style="font-size: 1.75rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 0; color: var(--text-main);">
            AI Machine-Readable Introspection Protocol
          </h2>
          <span class="docs-version-pill">nnui.ai.v1</span>
        </div>
        <p style="font-size: 1rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
          Every micro-enhancer implements the <code>nnui.ai.v1</code> introspection protocol. Autonomous AI agents (Cursor, Claude, Copilot, Antigravity) and developer tooling can query live element state and request copy-ready framework snippets at runtime:
        </p>
        <pre class="code-viewer-pre" style="border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);"><code>const element = document.querySelector('ui-data-grid');
const schema = await element.inspectAI();

console.log(schema.protocol);          // "nnui.ai.v1"
console.log(schema.schema.parts);      // ["toolbar", "search", "export-btn", "table", "pagination"]
console.log(schema.liveState);         // Active rows, sort column, search query
console.log(schema.frameworkSnippets); // Idiomatic React 19, Vue 3, Svelte 5 snippets</code></pre>

        <!-- AI Specification (llms.txt) Banner -->
        <div data-ui="card" style="margin-top: 1.5rem; background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.08) 0%, rgba(139, 92, 246, 0.04) 100%), var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.3); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1rem;">
          <div>
            <div style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-main); font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">
              🤖 Using Cursor, Copilot, or Claude? Use llms.txt
            </div>
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-muted);">
              Copy the standardized specification so your AI assistant writes 100% accurate NNUI-KIT code without hallucinations.
            </p>
          </div>
          <a href="/llms" data-ui="button" data-variant="primary" style="text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.85rem; padding: 0.5rem 1rem; border-radius: 6px; font-weight: 700;">
            View & Copy llms.txt →
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Framework Adapter: React 18 & 19 -->
      <section id="react" style="margin-bottom: 4rem;">
        <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
          <h2 style="font-size: 1.75rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 0; color: var(--text-main);">
            React 18 & 19 (Next.js 15 App Router)
          </h2>
          <span class="docs-version-pill" style="border-color: #3b82f6; color: #3b82f6;">First-Class Typed Wrappers</span>
        </div>
        <p style="font-size: 1rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
          NNUI-KIT provides official React 18 & 19 bindings exported from <code>nnui-kit/react</code>. Built with forward-ref semantics, TypeScript interfaces, and Next.js 15 App Router SSR safety:
        </p>

        <div style="border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 8px; background: var(--bg-card); overflow: hidden; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
          <div style="padding: 0.65rem 1rem; background: var(--bg-secondary); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 700;">
            app/dashboard/page.tsx
          </div>
          <pre class="code-viewer-pre" style="margin: 0;"><code>'use client';

import React, &#123; useState &#125; from 'react';
import 'nnui-kit/css';
import 'nnui-kit/client';
